# The owner state on the committed Ghidra projects, and on every scratch copy a
# driver makes of one, held by a check that reads committed text only.
# Prepared here rather than landed, for the reason
# docs/ci/agent-gates-capture-claims.patch gives:
# `.github/scripts/agent-gates.sh` is copied from the agent-pipeline template
# and the pipeline's push token has no `workflow` scope, so a branch editing it
# fails at the end of the PR rather than at the start of it.
#
# To land it:
#
#   git apply docs/ci/agent-gates-project-owner-gate.patch
#
# and that is the whole change.
#
# Added 2026-10-05, issue #572, which is the gate its own "done looks like"
# asked for and which nothing in the tree implemented. Two `python3` lines and no
# `gate` line: both top-level gaps a `check_*()` function could take are already
# cut against by other prepared patches -- the one between check_python_syntax()
# and check_ghidra_tooling()'s comment by agent-gates-bank-map-score.patch, the
# one before check_doc_links() by agent-gates-findings-frozen.patch -- so the
# call goes inside check_ghidra_tooling() on the two-line anchor this patch's
# header says, and `tools/test_agent_gates_patches.py`, which applies every
# ordered pair, is what holds that it composes. The shape is the one
# agent-gates-cross-decoder-disagreement.patch and
# agent-gates-0751-writer-census.patch already take for the same reason.
#
# Why the cheap tier: it reads the three committed `project.prp` files and parses
# two driver sources with `ast`. No firmware image, no Ghidra, no JVM, no
# network, no assembler, no PyYAML -- and it reads none of the `.rep` directories
# themselves, which are tens of megabytes of `-merge`-marked binary.
#
# What it buys. Every committed project records `VALUE="dave"` in its
# `project.prp`, and `analyzeHeadless` refuses a project owned by anyone else at
# the open, before a pre-script runs. `ghidra/project_owner.py`'s rewrite is what
# makes a disposable copy openable, and both drivers now preflight it before the
# run rather than aborting in a log -- but a preflight inside a driver cannot
# see the other driver, cannot see the third site, and goes away with the driver
# it lives in. This is the one place all three are visible together: a rewrite
# deleted from either driver's copy path, or a project that stopped recording an
# owner at all, is a red run here.
#
# What it does not establish. Nothing here claims a project opens, that the
# committed `.rep` survives a run byte-identical, or that the rewrite is
# *sufficient* rather than merely present in the copy path. Those are the
# drivers' `--self-test --oracle` and the run recorded in
# `docs/findings/ghidra-project-owner-gate.md`.
diff --git a/.github/scripts/agent-gates.sh b/.github/scripts/agent-gates.sh
index 16c70c3..037ea2b 100755
--- a/.github/scripts/agent-gates.sh
+++ b/.github/scripts/agent-gates.sh
@@ -120,6 +120,29 @@ check_ghidra_tooling() {
   # --check and --self-test need no Ghidra and no network, which is what lets
   # them live in a gate at all. A full rebuild does not, and is not here.
   #
+  # The owner state on the committed Ghidra projects, and on every scratch copy
+  # a driver makes of one. Cheap tier, like the call above: committed text only
+  # -- the three committed project.prp files and each driver's copy path -- so
+  # no image, no Ghidra and no JVM. `--check` is a property of the tree, and
+  # `--self-test` is the half that matters, because it is the refusals over
+  # fixtures written to be known-wrong and a check that has quietly stopped
+  # refusing looks exactly like a check that is working. What it buys: a
+  # rewrite_owner() dropped from a driver's export path, or a project that
+  # stopped recording an owner, is a red run here rather than a
+  # NotOwnerException in an analyzeHeadless log minutes downstream.
+  #
+  # **No `gate` line, and no `check_*()` wrapper.** Both top-level gaps a new
+  # function could take are already cut against: the one between
+  # check_python_syntax() and this function's comment belongs to
+  # agent-gates-bank-map-score.patch, and the one before check_doc_links() to
+  # agent-gates-findings-frozen.patch. Two `python3` lines here are what is
+  # left, and they are the shape agent-gates-cross-decoder-disagreement.patch and
+  # agent-gates-0751-writer-census.patch already take. The anchor is inside this
+  # function's own comment block rather than beside its `local rc=0` line, so
+  # tools/test_agent_gates_patches.py -- which applies every ordered pair --
+  # composes with both of those in either order.
+  python3 ghidra/check_project_owner_gate.py --check || rc=1
+  python3 ghidra/check_project_owner_gate.py --self-test || rc=1
   # Nothing in this loop turns on whether sdas8051 is installed, which is the
   # other half of the split. The sdas8051 re-encode used to run from here
   # whenever `command -v sdas8051` found the tool, and that made the gate's
